Tradewind is an independent, clean-room implementation. It is compatible with the
public API of backtrader but shares no code with it. Where its design follows
QuantConnect's Lean (Apache License 2.0), the attribution is recorded in this file.

Design attributions to QuantConnect Lean (https://github.com/QuantConnect/Lean,
Copyright QuantConnect Corporation, Apache License 2.0):

* spec/05-interfaces.md follows the decomposition of Lean's Security, SymbolProperties,
  SecurityHolding, CashBook, IFeeModel, IFillModel, ISlippageModel, IBuyingPowerModel,
  ISettlementModel, IShortableProvider, IMarginInterestRateModel, ISecurityPortfolioModel,
  SecurityChanges and SecurityExchangeHours, and the phase order of its
  AlgorithmManager time loop. The Python interfaces are Tradewind's own.
* src/tradewind/calendars.py and clock.ExchangeClock follow the shape of Lean's
  MarketHoursDatabase / SecurityExchangeHours (per exchange: time zone, weekly sessions,
  holidays, early closes) and its fill-forward of minute slices. The holiday rules and
  the code are Tradewind's own, written from the exchanges' published rules.
* spec/07-live-ibkr.md and src/tradewind/live/ follow two concepts of Lean's live trading:
  a brokerage behind one interface the algorithm never sees (IBrokerage), and a warm-up
  during which orders are refused. The Python code is Tradewind's own.

Optional dependency, not distributed with Tradewind: ib_async (BSD 2-Clause License,
https://github.com/ib-api-reloaded/ib_async), installed by the `ibkr` extra and imported
only by tradewind.live.ibkr when it connects.
